  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Identification of activities and partnerships for nature-based solutions and resilient cities in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mid-2023, a scoping study on the potential application of Water as Leverage has been investigated for the Mexican context. Due to limitations in terms of available time and budget, the focus of a future activity will be on a smaller-scale interventions, financed through the Thematic Approach of Partners for Water. The methodology of Water as Leverage focuses on bridging the gap between project origination and (financing) implementation, with an explicit focus on organising an inclusive process with involved and/or potentially affected stakeholders. This assignment requires an expert or expert team to be deployed, to identify opportunities to work with Mexican counterparts on the topic of nature-based solutions in cities. A focus will be on the city of Monterrey, but activities also include a professional review of other potential focus areas.</narrative>
  </description>
